      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:fd_scale",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00191",
        "x": 840,
        "y": 476,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "bin width 3.69   counts 1 to 42",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "xs",
          "color": "grey",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 370,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:fd_title",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00192",
        "x": 840,
        "y": 104,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Freedman-Diaconis: h = 2 IQR / n^(1/3) = 3.722, k = 14",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "green",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 370,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:fd_sub",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00193",
        "x": 840,
        "y": 420,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Both populations survive (2 local maxima) with no spurious spikes. Chosen as the shipped default because h is minimising an integrated squared error, not to look good.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "s",
          "color": "grey",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 370,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:edges",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00194",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 640,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Half-open bins: [a, b) on every bin, the last one closed on the right, so a value sitting exactly on an edge is counted once. Count it twice and the bars stop summing to n = 240.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "black",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1140,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:counter",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00195",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 686,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "The rule has a failure mode, and it is not cosmetic. Same n, seed 20261128, 0.55 N(28, 5) + 0.45 N(52, 6.5): the clusters are far apart, so IQR = 24.62 measures the separation instead of the width, h = 7.925, and FD returns k = 7 - COARSER than Sturges' 9. Bin rules are not ranked; each one is a bet about the shape.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "orange",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1140,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:degenerate",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00196",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 750,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "The edge case that breaks it outright: IQR = 0 makes h = 0 and k infinite. A constant column, or a majority tied on one value, has no bin width at all. Same class of failure as a correlation whose denominator is zero - the summary has no divisor, so it must refuse rather than default.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "red",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1140,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:fallback",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00197",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 812,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "So an implementation must refuse or fall back, and the week 4 cut rule says which: automatic binning drops to explicit edges only. Defaulting h would invent a distribution nobody measured. No binning ships in the Numerics lane (#28).",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "m",
          "color": "black",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1140,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      },
      {
        "typeName": "shape",
        "id": "shape:credit",
        "type": "text",
        "parentId": "page:page",
        "index": "a00198",
        "x": 40,
        "y": 874,
        "rotation": 0,
        "props": {
          "text": "Generated by make_tldr.py (quantiles: Hyndman-Fan type 7, the rule stateskol ships). The three assertions above run before the file is written, so this scene cannot claim a regime the data does not show.",
          "font": "draw",
          "size": "s",
          "color": "grey",
          "textAlign": "start",
          "verticalAlign": "start",
          "w": 1140,
          "autoSize": false,
          "scale": 1,
          "url": ""
        },
        "meta": {}
      }
    ]
  },
  "scope": "document"
}
